ew zealand  who said  or somewhere in new zealand who said  that the in english the ratio between  word families and words is 1.6 but i'm  not entirely clear on what a word family  is if we take i don't know act action  acting active  actor  is that a one word family or you know i  don't know  so i don't worry so i guess the other  thing is i just say to myself i need a  lot of words and i don't worry about how  many words i need  i know if i'm reading something if a  word is missing i've got to learn it  um  i might say this is perhaps an extremely  rare word and i won't worry about it but  then i don't deliberately try to learn  the words i simply save them at link  they're now highlighted in yellow if  that word appears again and again in  other texts again highlighted in yellow  i'll eventually get to know if if it  doesn't appear for six months i probably  didn't need that word so i don't worry  about it  um  so the key thing is that the word count  at link therefore  is more of a of a of a milestone it's  telling me when at times i may feel that  i'm not making progress in the language  it's telling me in fact you are because  you have accumulated all these words and  i know from experience when i have a  word count of 20 000 and say korean or  or romanian or some other language  if i find myself in a situation  where i have to speak a lot or i have an  opportunity to speak a lot i'm going to  improve very quickly that's what  happened to me when i was in romania  i i haven't spoken very much korean i'm  going to start speaking again i'm going  to speak with uh  my tutor joo hyun on on saturday  and and quite frankly i still have a lot  of trouble understanding  the bigger problem for me and language  earning is not how many words do i need  to know it's where do i find interesting  content that i like to read and like to  listen to and for korean still that is a  challenge the kim yong-ha series which  i've mentioned before is just that  little bit too difficult  and i understand quite well when he  talks  uh you know about literature but when he  actually reads excerpts from  yukio mishima or whatever i have a lot  of trouble following it and there's a  lot of  more difficult vocabulary in you know  straight from works of literature so  uh to me  i just worry about making sure i expose  myself to a lot of the language  and if i have a high word count that  link it tells me that i have been  exposing myself to a lot of the language  if i had been able to find content in  korean on current events with audio and  text  and a pleasant voice like  who's a  very pleasant person to listen to then  i'd probably have 40 000 words by now  because they would have been more  motivated to a lot to do a lot of that  listening really and that would mean  that i would understand better and when  i speak you'll i'll probably put up a  video at some point of my conversation  with ju hyun and i have trouble  understanding her because i simply  haven't done it very much i haven't  spoken much korean and so you need to  you need to uh to practice speaking but  you have to practice the speaking based  on  an ability to understand and that  ability to understand requires words how  many words exactly  i don't know for sure  i think in english 10 to 15 000 words  is that 25 000 words in korean  is it uh 20 30 000 words in russian or  czech i don't know but my own experience  has been that when i when i run into  trouble in the language  it's because i don't know the words  and you know in my progression you know  at first the language is just so much  noise  and then i'm able to separate out where  words end and the next you know one word  ends and the next word begins and pretty  soon i can identify i know exactly  that's a word i don't know as i'm  listening there's a word i don't know  there's a word i don't know and it's  it's the lack of vocabulary that  prevents me from understanding better  not sorting through the grammatical  structur